      "context": "Canonical layout alignment: this screen instances LWkpp (WorkbenchFamily/DevTools Text Transform), not a new Regex workbench family. Shared 56px full-width toolbar, 16px left workspace padding, stacked editor sections, right-hand settings-only panel, Generate/Update action directly below the prompt in the left pane, 40px full-width status bar and existing boundary treatments are retained. Normal desktop adaptation: 472px workbench height and 320px right panel, checked at 1366x768 and 1280x720. Primary verb: generate/refine regex from editable natural-language prompt; secondary verb: verify against arbitrary local sample. Preset dropdown retains Email, URL, IPv4, UUID, Hex color and Strong password; it fills the prompt without submitting. Example populates representative input; Reset confirms before clearing user work. Generate is disabled for whitespace-only prompt; Enter generates, Shift+Enter adds newline. Busy action becomes Stop. Failure uses shared retry toast and preserves inputs and previous result. Match/no-match and captured groups belong to the inline test surface; samples never go to AI. Random string is 16 ASCII letters/digits, not a guaranteed match. Editing sample invalidates earlier test feedback. Copy exports displayed literal only. Test timeout is bounded in a worker. Unsupported Python/PHP testing must not be mislabeled as JavaScript execution. New functionality still needs implementation. No New chat or external tester destination. Independent ui_validator and end_user_validator cannot be invoked with available session tools; their approval is pending. Explicit user correction: match shared workspace geometry only, not another tool’s action placement. Generate and Update belong directly below the prompt in the left workspace; do not put either action back in the settings panel. Manual test correction: every state shows Run test directly below its test editor. Before a valid regex exists it is disabled with Generate a regex first 