        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yiggN",
          "name": "Entry and live operation",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "LAYOUT & ENTRY  /  Use the existing ERY94 universal generator layout: expanded configuration above the full-width standard result surface. No custom cron result bar or right-side notes panel. Open with 0 9 * * 1-5, UTC and an empty label. Edit the five fields directly; update after 160 ms without Generate. Tab through the five fields, timezone and label, then the standard result-header actions.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Bd38p",
          "name": "Validation and recovery contract",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "VALIDATION  /  Keep attempted values visible. Associate inline errors with the affected input (aria-invalid + aria-describedby); use the helper line instead of an alert banner. While empty or invalid, replace the meaning with “Complete the highlighted fields to see your schedule”, hide the stale output and disable copy/download. On correction, restore the live result. Empty input is never treated as *. Announce settled validation politely, not on each keystroke.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "xXO5H",
          "name": "Syntax and edge cases",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "GRAMMAR  /  Standard five fields only. Minute 0–59; hour 0–23; day 1–31; month 1–12; weekday 0–7 (0 and 7 are Sunday). Accept numeric lists, ascending ranges, * and */n, matching the existing parser. Reject names, seconds, ?, L and range-with-step syntax. Both restricted day fields use OR. Syntax validity is not proof that a calendar date occurs. Long values remain editable with horizontal caret scrolling, never silently truncated.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "E2Id5",
          "name": "Artifact and settings contracts",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "SHARED OUTPUT LAYOUT  /  Reuse the existing full-width result surface, text renderer and header actions. Copy expression copies only the five-field line, preserving the previously designed behavior; Download .txt saves the expression, displayed description and optional timezone/label lines to cron-schedule.txt. No separate expression bar or duplicate artifact actions. UTC is implicit. Notes never change the host; the tool does not schedule jobs.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "a9RVm8",
          "name": "Feedback, presets and reset",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "FEEDBACK & RECOVERY  /  Use shared result actions and their success/error toasts. Copy success: “Expression copied”. Copy failure preserves selectable result text for manual copying. Download failure offers Retry. “Every 15 minutes” changes only five schedule fields; preserve timezone and label. Reset restores defaults and announces the reset. Reload starts at defaults; nothing is saved.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WIj65",
          "name": "Implementation gaps — explicit scope",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "IMPLEMENTATION DELTAS  /  Reuse the current generator and result layout, not cron-specific output chrome. Keep live configuration above the standard result surface. Preserve the proposed expression-only copy via the existing result-actions extension point. The clearer human description is a proposed describeCron improvement; show and download the same description. Until implemented, use its existing parser summary consistently. Field-local validation and guidance stay by the inputs; examples preserve notes.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Y4Rbx6",
          "name": "Viewport and acceptance checklist",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "DESKTOP REVIEW  /  1366×768 and 1280×720 use the same shared component, not separate output patterns. Core fields, notes and result-header actions remain in the initial viewport. Supporting sections scroll below. Check component identity, bounds, contrast, spacing, input/result accuracy and feedback/recovery. Mobile and live keyboard/clipboard behavior remain implementation tests.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ywZYA",
          "name": "Long expression and in-flight behavior",
          "fill": "$fg-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "LONG RESULTS & UPDATES  /  Use the existing text renderer: selectable output wraps inside a bounded scrollable content region; result-header actions stay visible. Copy expression retains exact expression bytes; Download retains exact complete result text. During debounce/validation, show the shared updating state and disable stale actions. Invalid input uses the shared result error state and field-local recovery; correction restores the live result.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-body",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
