            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "vsLAG",
              "name": "Comparison / Scope and handoff",
              "width": 2772,
              "fill": "$surface-muted",
              "cornerRadius": "$r-xl",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "FMBPG",
                  "name": "Direction comparison",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A — compact actions without losing calm focus. B — visual guidance first, form on the right. E — panoramic image with a practical input dock. F — a task-led sheet, not a marketing hero.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "h0yvd",
                  "name": "Cross-platform behavior",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The refined B design is applied to the YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, X and Facebook flows above. Each uses AmvWB with platform-specific labels, supported-link hints, restrictions and illustration proportions. Existing selection, preparation, download and recovery states remain in their platform groups.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "IDS2T",
                  "name": "Operation and recovery",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Paste or type a public link → Find video → existing retrieval state → source preview and available-file selection → prepare → browser download. B: Find video is the only button beside the input. Paste through the native field interaction; no clipboard permission is required. Clear appears below the field, only when it contains text. Find video previews availability, not an immediate download. Invalid links retain text and replace field helper text with an actionable error. Long links scroll inside the standard 44px input. No quality controls before retrieval. F’s future rows are explanatory, not clickable stages.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vCiAZ",
                  "name": "Responsive handoff",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Applied design: each platform group contains its refined desktop entry, a 1280 × 720 laptop entry, and a 390 × 844 mobile entry alongside the existing selection and download stages. Desktop keeps the left illustration; mobile hides it entirely, stacks the standard input and full-width Find video action, and keeps platform restrictions inline. Previous entry screens and task surfaces are preserved in the disabled archive.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "O3pHR",
                  "name": "Review scope",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Rollout self-review: each platform’s desktop and laptop entry is grouped with its existing flow; mobile hides the left guide and retains the standard input with one full-width primary action. New entries checked for clipping at 1366 × 768, 1280 × 720 and mobile widths 390 / 375. Existing downstream states are preserved, not redesigned in this rollout. Independent ui_validator and end_user_validator agents remain unavailable; their review is pending.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "zZUfo",
          "name": "09 / Reference — research & developer notes",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "j094pW",
              "name": "Section title",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "content": "09 / Reference — not product UI",
              "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
              "fontSize": 28,
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GpN7L",
              "name": "Scope and status",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "PROPOSED PRODUCT • Five dedicated tools: YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, X and Facebook. Public-video retrieval only. Platform support and file availability must be verified before launch.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 20,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "JiKEJ",
              "name": "Research evidence",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "OBSERVED ONLINE\nSSSTik (ssstik.io/en): prominent paste / clear / download; Share → Copy link instructions; public-account limitation and browser download-folder help.\nPubler (publer.com/tools/video-downloader): one URL entry across platforms, example-link guidance and explicit issue reporting.\nCobalt (github.com/imputnet/cobalt): “paste the link, get the file, move on”; public-content-only ethics and clear proxy model. About page separates settings from the save task.\nResearch limitation: Cobalt live canvas render was blank; SnapInsta and FDown returned access blocks. No successful download transactions were tested.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "FEoZL",
              "name": "What to adopt and reject",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "ADOPT  Link-first entry, clipboard convenience with manual fallback, clear source verification, progressive disclosure of formats, browser-save help.\nAVOID  Advertising-style download buttons, guaranteed “HD / unlimited / no watermark”, asking for social credentials, calling remote retrieval “local”, or claiming a file is already saved.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "HdKWi",
              "name": "Operation model and feasibility",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "OPERATION CONTRACT\nSave a permitted public video → paste its share URL → resolve and verify the actual clip → choose an available file → prepare → Download file. Portrait clips stay portrait; landscape videos stay landscape; multi-video posts expose selectable previews. Source and preview live left; format settings, preparation feedback and output actions live right. Recovery keeps the URL editable.\nLAUNCH GATES  Backend owner: platform/domain allowlist, safe redirect resolution and SSRF protection, format metadata, transfer/expiry limits, cancellation and error taxonomy. Product/legal owner: platform terms, copyright policy, supported regions and retention disclosure. Availability examples are design fixtures, not a claim of implemented support.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "A6hgEK",
              "name": "Review matrix and evidence limits",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 2800,
              "content": "REVISION CHECKLIST\nNon-overlapping flow groups · Shared selected/unselected states · Essential screen copy only · Desktop/laptop/mobile preserved.\nLong research and implementation notes live here, outside product screens. Screenshots of the revised hub and shared selection states captured; independent review requested.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "a3RLa",
              "name": "Responsive discovery handoff",
              "width": 760,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 20,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "XRHaQ",
                  "name": "Mobile viewport",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "MOBILE VIEWPORT\n390 px full-page design. At 844 px viewport height, the link field, Paste link, Find video and the start of the directory are visible. The remainder scrolls vertically.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U8NcF",
                  "name": "Laptop viewport",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "LAPTOP VIEWPORT\n1280 × 720 variant keeps the complete entry form and five-platform directory visible. Use fewer directory columns when titles need more room, rather than smaller text.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "sCMr7",
                  "name": "Navigation contract",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "NAVIGATION CONTRACT\nDownloaders is a new ecosystem destination. The prototype shows it active. Preserve access to all tools through the SmartTools logo and global search; other existing product destinations remain available.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ZvbAb",
                  "name": "More platforms",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "MORE PLATFORMS\nDo not list “all websites” or expose dead tool cards. Add further platforms only after the retrieval adapter and platform-specific flow are supported and reviewed.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "qnxeK",
              "name": "Hub transition handoff",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 2800,
              "content": "ENTRY → Direct /downloaders, shared navigation or platform card. Find video detects the allowed platform and opens its source-selection step with the submitted URL retained. Platform cards open dedicated empty tools. Paste reads clipboard only on click; denial keeps typing/pasting available. Empty submit → required-field error. Refresh starts empty; no URL is stored in navigation history. Mobile page scrolls vertically; input + Find video remain in the first viewport.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "k02HE",
              "name": "Remaining transitions",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "CANCEL → abort active request and return to editable link; ignore stale responses. CHANGE URL → invalidate old source, options and output. CHANGE QUALITY → keep source; invalidate prepared file. NETWORK FAILURE → floating error + Retry; never erase the URL. RATE LIMIT → toast states server-provided retry time; show Retry when allowed. CLIPBOARD DENIED → explain “Paste with Ctrl/Cmd+V or touch and hold”; keep field focus. DOWNLOAD REQUESTED → keep Download again available; say “Check your browser downloads”, never “Saved to your device”. iPhone preview → browser Share → Save to Files. Reload starts a new session; no saved history. Unsupported login-only or protected content → explain limitation; never request credentials.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "dko8i",
              "name": "Implementation accessibility contract",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Keyboard: URL → Paste → Find → available options → Prepare → Download. Announce lookup/preparation status without moving focus; focus the source title after lookup and result heading when prepared. Prevent double submit; label progress only when real bytes are known. No fabricated percentage. Long titles wrap to two lines with full title available in the source link; filenames wrap. Preview failure keeps source title, duration and Open source usable.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "cX4OA",
              "name": "URL validation implementation note",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "URL validation: keep field editable, associate and announce the error, focus the field on invalid submit.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "oyR2E",
              "name": "Operation contract and scope",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1366,
              "content": "Save a public video → paste link → verify portrait preview / choose video → select a source file → download. Preview and selection stay left; quality and file handoff stay right. Illustrative media and file metadata, not a live retrieval. Shared errors and hub are owned by the main flow.",
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 15,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "wKSUB",
              "name": "Developer handoff / transitions, source contract and recovery",
              "width": 1366,
              "fill": "$surface-muted",
              "cornerRadius": "$r-md",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "olmvT",
                  "name": "Handoff heading",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Behavior contract · applies to both complete flows",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 22,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Sj1tE",
                  "name": "Entry and lookup",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Paste uses clipboard permission; if denied, keep the input editable and show “Paste your link manually”. Trim whitespace; Clear empties the field. Find validates the platform URL, then announces “Finding video…” with Cancel. Empty/invalid links stay beside the field. Shared errors/toasts are owned by the main session.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "sf69p",
                  "name": "Source truth and branch",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Public links are sent to the server; never request credentials or bypass private access. Unsupported or unavailable posts use the shared recovery pattern. Offer only returned formats, dimensions and audio states; do not promise HD, watermark removal, MP3 or unlimited access. The displayed files and photography are illustrative fixtures, not verified platform responses.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "P4KKA",
                  "name": "TikTok selection",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "TikTok: 720p selected; 480p available. File choices are one radio group using BlwMt. Whole row activates the choice; lower resolution reduces storage. Source files may retain watermarks. Prepare disables repeat submission and announces “Preparing file…”; Cancel returns to selection. Change quality invalidates the prepared file.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "p4kHWK",
                  "name": "Instagram selection",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Instagram: shared checkboxes independently toggle videos; selected cards use accent-soft and accent borders. First video selected initially; fixture shows 1 and 3 selected. Zero selected disables Prepare with “Select at least one video”. Each video has its own radio group: video 1 offers 720p / 480p; video 3 offers 1080p / 720p. Single Reel omits multi-select count; exclude photos.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wMbaO",
                  "name": "Handoff and recovery",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Preparation produces one MP4 per selected video, not a ZIP. Show actual filename, bytes, dimensions, duration and audio state when known; omit unknown sizes rather than estimate. Download starts a browser save, not proof of a saved file. Use the shared toast for download failure and keep Retry available. Partial preparation keeps successful files and Retry on failed files.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "yq9f7",
                  "name": "Back, re-entry and privacy",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Change link returns to editable entry with the previous URL, clearing previous selection and results only after a new lookup. Cancel preserves link and quality. Within-page back preserves selections. A fresh visit starts empty; do not imply server retention or durable results. Never claim local-only processing.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "o1j84",
                  "name": "Implementation and validation owners",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Backend owner must confirm resolver support, availability, preparation and artifact contracts before implementation. Main flow owns hub and shared loading/error/retry visuals. Required ui_validator and end_user_validator agents are not exposed in this session; independent approval remains pending.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Tnqfj",
                  "name": "Responsive contract and verification checklist",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "RESPONSIVE · 1366 × 768 desktop and 1280 × 720 laptop retain two columns. Mobile 390px stacks media then settings; Prepare follows the selected count, with available qualities below. Height beyond 844px documents vertical scroll, not a larger viewport.\nREVIEW · Current screenshots inspected for task fit, novice feasibility, five-second scan, feedback/recovery, alignment, contrast and clipping. Laptop clipped action corrected. Both repo validator definitions read; no agent runner is exposed, so independent approval remains pending. Main session owns parent board placement.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "mBp1m",
                  "name": "Relocated usage guidance",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "USAGE · In TikTok or Instagram: Share → Copy link. Paste here, preview, choose source files, prepare, then download. Downloads use the browser save location (Downloads / Files on phones). Preview playback verifies the source; files and photography are illustrative. UI keeps labels, media facts, brief status and the next action; explanatory copy stays here.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "WnuMo",
              "name": "Operation contract",
              "fill": "$fg-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Public link → choose clip and file → prepare → download. Source left; settings and output right.",
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "s6q8Fh",
              "name": "X & Facebook / developer handoff, research and validation status",
              "width": 1366,
              "fill": "$surface",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 12,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "VgHgq",
                  "name": "Handoff · explicit state transitions",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Handoff · explicit state transitions",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "cuR9L",
                  "name": "Handoff · explicit state transitions specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "X: choose one clip using the shared radio control (44px row, 16px indicator). Selecting clip 2 updates its still, duration and available files and clears any prepared file. One selected file per clip; Prepare download uses that clip and file. Selection remains editable after preparation; changing it returns to file selection. Facebook has one returned Reel, so no clip selector is shown. No download-all or invented quality tiers.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ALm2a",
                  "name": "Server work and recovery · use shared states owned by the main session",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Server work and recovery · use shared states owned by the main session",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JTgqL",
                  "name": "Server work and recovery · use shared states owned by the main session specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Find videos → Checking public link… → returned source and files. Prepare download → Preparing file on our server… → file ready. Use indeterminate progress, not invented percentages. While busy, disable duplicate submission and offer Cancel. Cancel returns to the previous editable state. Network/preparation errors use the shared toast and Retry; retain URL and selection.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "BETwE",
                  "name": "Validation and access limits",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Validation and access limits",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "W8d1e",
                  "name": "Validation and access limits specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Empty or malformed URL: field-associated error. Trim pasted whitespace; accept supported X/twitter post links and Facebook video/Reel share links only. Resolve redirects server-side and revalidate the destination. No credentials, cookies, private access or login bypass. An inaccessible public link uses the shared unavailable state; Change link returns to editable URL input.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "t1Jn9U",
                  "name": "File truth and handoff",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "File truth and handoff",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ZIauK",
                  "name": "File truth and handoff specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Files, dimensions, container and sound labels come from the source response. With sound / No sound / Sound unknown must remain explicit; never infer audio from MP4. Sizes are shown only when known after preparation. No upscaling, guaranteed resolution or speed promise. The sample illustrates 720p/360p, not a fixed menu. Facebook standard videos retain their source aspect ratio; Reels remain portrait. All preview photography, links and file values are illustrative fixtures, not live availability claims. Production previews use retrieved source media.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wu4v2",
                  "name": "Completion and re-entry",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Completion and re-entry",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "PKJFV",
                  "name": "Completion and re-entry specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Download MP4 requests the prepared file and invokes browser saving; do not claim it was saved. Download failure retains the prepared result and offers Retry via shared toast. Choose another file/clip returns to selection and clears the old prepared result. Change link clears source and file choices. Re-entry starts at URL input; do not promise persisted links or files.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GyeXI",
                  "name": "Responsive and accessible implementation",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Responsive and accessible implementation",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "woILa",
                  "name": "Responsive and accessible implementation specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "1366 × 768 desktop baseline and 1280 × 720 laptop evidence are above. At 390px the same shell uses shared mobile navigation, stacked source → file panel, wrapping URLs and vertical document scrolling. Core selection and primary action remain reachable; no horizontal scroll. Use labelled radio groups, keyboard clip selection, 44px actions, visible focus and live status announcements. Mobile full-page height is not viewport height.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "GJ1wN",
                  "name": "Research and independent review status",
                  "fill": "$fg-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Research and independent review status",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 18,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xePHE",
                  "name": "Research and independent review status specification",
                  "fill": "$fg-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Review: all 14 desktop, laptop and mobile screens captured after in-place simplification. Bounds check: no visible clipping or unintended sibling overlaps; shared logo layers intentionally overlap. Problem fit, novice entry, five-second scan, and feedback/recovery inspected across both flows. Fixtures are illustrative; backend support remains unverified. Independent ui_validator and end_user_validator runs remain blocked: no delegation tool or codex executable in this session. This is not an independent PASS.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "I2iU7D",
