            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "smZec",
              "name": "Initial-state research — broader comparison and decisions",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1800,
              "content": "INITIAL ENTRY / COMPARATIVE RESEARCH\nSnapTik — live screenshot + page text: prominent link field and three-step copy/paste/download. Adopt direct entry; reject ad gaps and blanket HD/no-watermark claims.\nSSSTik — page text: Paste/Clear and Share → Copy link guidance. Adopt clipboard recovery and short source-specific help.\nFastDl — live screenshot + page text: content-type navigation and illustrated copy/paste instructions. Adopt Reel/post distinction and visual guidance; avoid gradient-heavy promotion and unsupported content types.\nTwitterVideoDownloader — live screenshot + page text: post URL, Paste, and source-link explanation. Adopt post-level guidance; reject the large empty ad area above the field.\nSaveVideo — page text: an example URL and source-dependent format/quality explanation. Adopt recognizable supported-link patterns and defer format selection until retrieval.\nCobalt — page text: lean link-first actions. Keep the task short, without hiding limitations.\nVEED — page text: direct entry, fair-use cue, and ordered workflow. Keep permission disclosure; do not import its editing workflow.\nFDown / SnapInsta — access blocked (403); not treated as reviewed UI. No downloader transaction was tested.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "GOUmt",
              "name": "Guided entry interaction and acceptance contract",
              "fill": "$fg-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1800,
              "content": "GUIDED ENTRY / HANDOFF\nFind video validates the field, retrieves the source, then opens the existing selection state. Empty or invalid URLs retain focus and use the shared inline field-error pattern; service errors use the shared toast. Paste link requests clipboard access on click only; denial keeps manual paste available. Clear empties the field and restores focus. The right-hand example is non-interactive copy-link guidance, never a retrieved source or a successful result. No network request occurs while simply viewing the page.\nOperation: supply a public link → confirm source and available files → save. Entry teaches link acquisition only; quality and clip selection stay in the next state. Desktop actions are content-sized. Mobile Find video fills the row, with Paste/Clear secondary below. Shared M0akV input sizing is unchanged. Initial screens and source/result stages remain grouped per platform.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 14,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
